While the critical points of the loss landscape in linear neural networks have been extensively studied since the seminal work of Baldi \& Hornik in the late 1980s, a description of this landscape at an intermediate or global scale is still lacking. Such a characterization is crucial, particularly as a substantial body of literature indicates that gradient descent circumvents critical points.
Identifies and characterizes 'channels to infinity' in neural loss landscapes where weights diverge but loss decreases. ... Establishes error bounds and linear convergence for the regularized loss of deep linear networks.
A survey of gradient flow dynamics and loss landscape properties for deep linear neural networks.
